This directory vendors example payloads copied verbatim from external specifications, for use as
test fixtures. No source code from these projects is included.

x402 v2 protocol examples
  Source: https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402
  Commit: c84154b5d6a31d77fd5b9dbb01213053fd9cb9eb (main, fetched 2026-09-28)
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Files:
    payment-required.json           specs/x402-specification-v2.md, section 5.1.1
    payment-payload.json            specs/transports-v2/http.md, "Payment Payload Transmission"
                                     (identical to the exact-scheme/eip3009 example in
                                     specs/schemes/exact/scheme_exact_evm.md)
    settlement-response-success.json  specs/x402-specification-v2.md, section 5.3.1
    settlement-response-failure.json  specs/transports-v2/http.md, "Settlement Response Delivery"
    verify-response-success.json      specs/x402-specification-v2.md, section 7.1 ("Successful Response")
    verify-response-error.json        specs/x402-specification-v2.md, section 7.1 ("Error Response")

  See also Eip3009TypedDataTest#matchesTheX402SpecPaymentPayloadKnownAnswer, which decodes
  payment-payload.json above and asserts the recovered signer, the EIP-712 domain separator and
  the TransferWithAuthorization typehash all match values independently confirmed against the
  live USDC contract on Base Sepolia (see Eip3009DomainSeparatorLiveTest, @Tag("testnet")).

EIP-712 "Mail" example vector
  Source: https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-712
  License: CC0 1.0 Universal
  File: eip712-mail-example.json
    The `TypedData` request parameter from the "Specification of the eth_signTypedData JSON RPC"
    example. The expected result in that example,
    0x4355c47d63924e8a72e509b65029052eb6c299d53a04e167c5775fd466751c9d07299936d304c153f6443dfa05f40ff007d72911b6f72307f996231605b915621c,
    is the signature produced by the well-known "cow" test private key (keccak256("cow")); see
    Eip712MailVectorTest, which recomputes and asserts it via the same web3j StructuredDataEncoder
    machinery Eip3009TypedData itself is built on (not the "Mail" struct type itself, which this
    starter never encodes -- only the fixed TransferWithAuthorization struct).
